request: In the watchlist, show movies I haven't watched yet before the ones I've watched.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist  (The request is a display-ordering rule for the watchlist page: unwatched movies before watched ones. The watchlist component's `movies` signal is what its template renders, so a stable sort there (watched items last) satisfies it without changing the store's contract or any other consumer (app, search, movie-detail). No exported signature changes. The acceptance test seeds a real store with watched and unwatched items interleaved (so a missing sort fails whether the store appends or prepends) and pins both the `movies` signal order and the rendered DOM order.)
round 1: owners watchlist=ok; oracle RED
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 1 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (tsc is clean; of the 3 failures, two are watchlist's own toggle tests (regressed by the round-1 ordering change), so only watchlist is implicated. The third failure (NG0201: no ActivatedRoute) was my acceptance test's fault — it created Watchlist without router providers while the template uses RouterLink — so I am fixing/extending that test myself and re-instructing the watchlist owner to restore the failing toggling behaviour without touching existing tests, while keeping the unwatched-first order.)
round 2: owners watchlist=fail; oracle RED
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 1 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 3: plan -> watchlist  (Round 2 never took effect: the owner's submission was discarded at validation (testChangeReasons[1] missing its required title), so no test-change request ever reached me and I have nothing I can approve yet (the tooling confirmed those titles are not registered requests). The repo is still in the round-1 state: the unwatched-first implementation is correct (my acceptance test passes) and only the two positionally-pinned click tests fail. I will re-instruct the owner to first try non-test-change fixes, and if the tests genuinely pin the old order, to submit a properly-formed change request so the approval cycle can proceed next round.)
round 3: owners watchlist=rejected; oracle RED
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 1 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 4: plan -> watchlist  (The suite was green before round 1; since then the only behavioural change is the user-requested unwatched-first ordering, which my acceptance test verifies is correctly implemented (tsc clean, no other failures). The two red toggle tests locate their target row positionally and therefore pin the pre-change rendered order, which the user's request intentionally invalidates. Approving modification of exactly those two tests, constrained to keep the real click interaction and the watched-toggle assertion while locating the target row by the movie it renders instead of by position.)

